  "text_md": "## Cont.. (distribution time)\n\n## In PZP architecture:\n\n- In P2P, when a peer receives some file data, it can use its own upload capacity to redistribute the data to other peers.\n\nCalculating the distribution time for the PZP architecture is somewhat more complicated. 4 simple expression for the minimal distribution time:\n\n- Stepl: At the beginning, only the server has the file.\n- To get this file into the community of peers, minimum distribution time is at least Flus\n- Step2: the peer with the lowest download rate cannot obtain all F bits of the file in less than F/dmin seconds.\n- Step3: the total upload capacity of the system is, = Utotal\n- The system must deliver (upload) F bits to each of the N peers.\n- This cannot be done at a rate faster than Utotal'\n- So, the minimum distribution time is also at least NF/(us + u1 +\n- Finally; the minimum distribution time for P2P\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- image -->",
